= Modules
[[115]edit]
The ESP32 PICO [116]system in package modules combine an
ESP32 silicon chip, crystal oscillator, flash memory chip,
filter capacitors, and RF matching links into a single 7
mm × 7 mm sized QFN package.
The first released PICO was the ESP32-PICO-D4 with 2 CPUs
at 240 MHz, 4MiB internal flash, a 40 MHz oscillator and
34 GPIOs.[6]
Later, in 2020, the ESP32-PICO-V3 and ESP32-PICO-V3-02
modules were introduced both based on the ESP32 ECO V3
wafer.[7][8]
In 2022 the ESP32-S3-PICO-1 module was introduced with USB
OTG and internal PSRAM.[9]
