= Surface-mount module boards
[[120]edit]
ESP32 based [121]surface-mount [122]printed circuit board
modules directly contain the ESP32 [123]SoC and are
designed to be easily integrated onto other circuit
boards. Meandered [124]inverted-F antenna designs are used
for the PCB trace antennas on the modules listed below. In
addition to flash memory, some modules include
[125]pseudostatic RAM (pSRAM).
Vendor Name Antenna Flash memory ([126]MiB) PSRAM
([127]MiB) Description
Espressif ESP-WROOM-03 PCB trace 4 0 Discontinued. Limited
distribution, pre-production module created by Espressif
for beta testing purposes; this module used the ESP31B,
the beta testing chip for the ESP32
series.[11][12][13][14][15] FCC Part 15.247 tested (FCC
ID: 2AC7Z-ESP32).[16]
ESP32-WROOM-32 First publicly available ESP32 module board
created by Espressif.[17] FCC Part 15.247 tested (FCC ID:
2AC7Z-ESPWROOM32).[18] Based on ESP32-D0WDQ6 chip.
Originally named "ESP-WROOM-32".
ESP32-WROOM-32E 4,8,16 Same as ESP32-WROOM-32 but with the
Eco V3 processor revisions[19]
ESP32-WROOM-32D 4 Revision of the ESP-WROOM-32 module
which uses an ESP32-D0WD chip instead of an ESP32-D0WDQ6
chip.[20] Originally named "ESP-WROOM-32D".
ESP32-SOLO-1 Similar to the ESP32-WROOM-32D module, but
uses the single-core ESP32-S0WD chip instead of the
dual-core ESP32-D0WD.
ESP32-WROOM-32U [128]U.FL socket Alternative to the
ESP-WROOM-32D module which has a U.FL connector for
external antenna in lieu of a PCB trace antenna.[20]
ESP32-WROVER PCB trace 4 ESP32 module board with 4 MiB
pSRAM created by Espressif. FCC part 15.247 tested (FCC ID
2AC7Z-ESP32WROVER). Uses 40 MHz crystal oscillator. Does
not include U.FL connector. Based on ESP32-D0WDQ6 chip.
Since June 2018, new modules have been upgraded to 8 MiB
pSRAM.
ESP32-WROVER-I U.FL socket, PCB trace Variation of
ESP32-WROVER module configured to use an on-board U.FL
